CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ int has no tail: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ long long: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
expected constant expression
--
In a template, `[]() { ... }()' calls the function the lambda is lowered
to, which was not treated as constexpr and whose body was not typed as a
converted function body, so the call did not fold and `cond<tail, T>' had
no constant argument.
